On 2005-11-03, Marky Mark wrote:
> I remember hearing something about the pros and cons of both
> invisibility and displacement, and that if you are invisible and
> displaced, that you will not get the benefits from displacement?
>
> Was just wondering if that last statement is true, and if so, which is
> better, invisibility or displacement?
>
> Just that Ive got my first slashem character that looks like he can
> ascend (Im only dlv 25 or so, but I cant see what can stop me), and I
> want to make sure nothing goes wrong. Currently he is wearing a claok
> of displacement, but has just found a blessed potion of invisibility,
> was wondering if I should go for the permenant invisibility or stay
> visible and displaced.
>
IIRC, invisibility overrides displacement, yes. The effect of
displacement is better in that it can make the monsters think you were
two squares away from where you actually are, as opposed to one square
for invisibility. Invisibility has the drawback that you cannot enter
shops (cure: mummy wrapping). Displacement can only be gained by the
cloak, which has a magic cancellation value of 2, making it hard
(impossible?) to get MC###. Some say MC## isn't too bad in most cases,
some won't take a step into the valley without MC###. Plus you won't be
able to wear a CoMR, or a CoProtection which is nice (and also MC###)
when you get MR from something(s) else.

I'd personally suggest you stick to the CoDis at least until you find a
better option for the cloak slot. That !oInvis won't evaporate, so you
might as well stash it until then.

